# Detection 1: Excessive DNS queries by endpoint
# Detects a sudden base rate increase in DNS requests from a single endpoint.
# Why it matters: DNS tunneling often produces large query spikes.
# Fields required: _time, host, src_ip, query_name, count
# MITRE ATT&CK: T1071.004 (Application Layer Protocol)
# Analyst triage: review host, user, and response patterns; compare with baseline.

index=dns_analytics
| stats count AS query_count BY host, src_ip
| where query_count > 200
| sort - query_count
